ight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " One sec Exactly. Just to clarify, we don't need to wake every seat just because it's on screen. DevPad can show a terminal that's really just a separate live process. We can keep your important ones hot and just eliminate the window sprawl. The savings come from killing duplicate UI shells and not from suspending the terminals you rely on. DevPad is one visual shell over many terminals, and we can decide later which lanes are allowed to sleep, but your core ones can just stay live.", "text_chars": 487, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cb002cf2-8f20-4a99-8013-5ddfca75bff5", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790259354.4856553, "updated_at": 1790259400.56035, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " That's what I thought so the yeah so but again- that orc- so hold on a second though. There is a tax, though, because think about it from a monitor perspective, at a video card. If they're on one window then me opening and dragging around eight is less tax on the video card than one window", "text_chars": 291, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "763be691-c7e8-4b29-8399-183f1ae86f71", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790259356.653655, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Hmm", "text_chars": 4, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unext