re stuck\" moment into a quick swap, instead of a late night war room.", "text_chars": 365, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "898e7840-455a-4c75-bb84-5c249e9294fe", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790259680.5816445, "updated_at": 1790259789.49643, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " All right, now let's talk through the next thing on my mind Right- aaaand I'll do some research as we get- or we just talk through it. Is The next big thing on my mind is I- I understand the limitations. With trying to embed a web browser Right Into our Dev Pad. I understand that. Right, but the bigger picture is Me and you work in isolation for a res- for a reason. But You're still a main part of the hands-on orchestration for every project, whether it's ad hoc, whatever. You're getting no PTO as they joked around. And we're doing prompts back and forth where I'm copying. Right? So what are we gonna do for our cable car? Right? I think Google Drive is is too much of a fucking Like it's gonna be not a mess but connected. It's like too many hops, right? Because you're telling me you're- we're gonna need you to make a prompt, right? Then you're gonna save it And then we're gonna- actually it might work all right because if the MCP inbox works then the Google Drive could probably work quick. Right? It's when you make your handoffs, you go boom. Luce do this. Boom, Luce do this. Boom, Luce do this. We just got to make that structure in Google Drive", "text_chars": 1163, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1cbba9e7-889b-4d99-9108-b9c7dd34de04", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at"