chitect** in the current pool. Nex Pro is the safest substitute because it will stop where evidence stops instead of inventing architecture. |\n| **3 Vittorio** | Technical advisor / challenge / warboard | **Dots3 Note Preview Free** | Strongest validated free anomaly hunter. Good at finding the weird thing everybody else missed and challenging the prevailing read. |\n| **4 Nico** | Implementation hammer / builder | **MiMo-V2.6-Flash Free** *field trial* | Not validated by the old Black Pearl trial—the artifact tested MiMo V2, not 2.6—but **our current operational experience is materially better with 2.6 Flash**. This is exactly what Rookie should pressure-test. |\n| **5 VoiceBridge** | Voice/service lane | **No model substitution** | VoiceBridge is infrastructure, not a cognitive seat. Rookie should point to the same service or an isolated test instance—not assign an LLM just to fill the square. |\n| **6 Luce** | Verification / ground truth | **Big Pickle** if promo-free remains available; otherwise **Nex N2.5 Mini Free** | Big Pickle already earned the verification/truth-checking berth. Nex Mini is the best current fallback: excellent missing-data restraint and low storytelling. |\n| **7 Talon** | Operations / sequencing / routing | **Muse Spark 1.3 Free** | Clean, disciplined, restrained. Strong cross-workstream pattern recognition without trying to become the architect. Very good fit for “what happens next?” |\n| **8 Keel** | Build/deploy / operational execution | **MiMo-V2.6-Flash Free** *provisional* | Same reason as Nico, but with a tighter bounded deployment brief. We need a fresh code/build trial before promoting this as proven. |\n| **9 Falcon** | Data acquisition / retrieval | **Qwen3.8 27B Free** | The Black Pearl labor map specifically left Qwen in the **gathering/retrieval candidate** lane. The earlier trial was rate-limited rather than a model-quality failure. This is exactly where I would retest it. |\n\n### Rookie board I would actually boot\n\n```text\n┌────────────────────┬────────────────────┬────────────────────┐\n│ 1 CODA             │ 2 CHIAVE           │ 3 VITTORIO         │\n│ Nex N2.5 Pro       │ Nex N2.5 Pro       │ Dots3 Note Preview │\n├────────────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────┤\n│ 4 NICO             │ 5 VOICEBRIDGE      │ 6 LUCE             │\n│ MiMo V2.6 Flash    │ Service            │ Big Pickle*        │\n│                    │                    │ Nex Mini fallback  │\n├────────────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────┤\n│ 7 TALON            │ 8 KEEL             │ 9 FALCON           │\n│ Muse Spark 1.3     │ MiMo V2.6 Flash    │ Qwen3.8 27B       │\n└────────────────────┴────────────────────┴────────────────────┘\n```\n\n`*` assuming the Big Pickle free/promo route is still live when Rookie launches.\n\n## The interesting part: duplicates are fine\n\nI **wouldn't force nine different models** just to make Rookie look diverse.\n\nIf Nex Pro is our strongest free grounded brain, then having it occupy both **Coda and provisional Chiave** is completely consistent with:\n\n> **MODEL != SEAT**\n\nSame model, different bootstrap, different seat authority, different job.\n\nLikewise MiMo can occupy **Nico + Keel** while we're testing whether V2.6 Flash is actually a dependable implementation family.\n\nThat itself becomes useful research: *does the same runtime behave differently when loaded into Nico vs Keel doctrine?*\n\n## Where I would *not* waste Rookie slots\n\nBased on Black Pearl evidence:\n\n**Nemotron 3.5 Lightning** — prior ~10-minute latency plus missing-game/data errors. Not worth a persistent seat.\n\n**Nemotron 3 Ultra** — too much gap filling / speculation for trusted work.\n\n**Laguna XS 2.1** — major logic/data errors. We already saw enough.\n\n**LFM2.5-2.6B** — maybe someday for dirt-cheap routing/classification, but not a working seat.\n\n**North Mini Code** — interesting name for Nico, but our actual trial failed provenance/artifact expectations. I wouldn't promote it because it says “Code.”\n\n**Inkling** — needs a clean identity test before we know what we actually have.\n\n### Two rookies I *do* want on the bench\n\n**Muse Spark 1.2** = first reserve.  \nIt wasn't as clean as 1.3, but it performed well enough to earn a second-interview/reserve designation.\n\n**Ling 3.0 Flash Fin** = specialist reserve.  \nNot trusted for primary grounded work, but its market-structure curiosity was interesting enough to keep around for deliberately bounded challenge work. fileciteturn3file0\n\nSo I'd define Rookie as **9 active slots + bench**, not “nine free models and we're done.”\n\nAnd the biggest unresolved slot is **Chiave**. We have no free model that has demonstrated the architectural/integration behavior GLM 5.1 demonstrated. I would deliberately mark Rookie Chiave:\n\n> **NEX PRO — ACTING / PROVISIONAL**\n\nrather than pretending we solved that substitution. memcite", "text_chars": 5928, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9977b862-21ff-4492-8726-7a0147172704", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790261854.072, "updated_at": 1790261870.888176, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "ok we need to use another model for seat 9 unfortunatoley qwen iusa always rate limited", "text_chars": 87, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "758ea636-2ee1-4878-a24d-d6946aed46d0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790261861.887365, "updated_at": 1790261861.887365, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks":