s in-scope.\n- LAN-IP plain HTTP clipboard behavior is OUT OF SCOPE.\n\nLUCE GATE STATUS:\nLuce must first provide behavioral evidence.\n\nIf Luce reports:\nCLIPBOARD BEHAVIOR VERIFIED — NO ADDITIONAL CODE CHANGE REQUIRED\n\nSTOP.\nMAKE NO CHANGES.\n\nIf Luce reports a reproducible failure, proceed only against that exact failure.\n\n==================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nFix only the reproduced clipboard/focus defect with the smallest possible client-side change.\n\nPRIMARY ALLOWED CHANGE SURFACE:\npublic\\renderer.js\n\nDo not broaden scope unless direct reproduction proves the failure is outside renderer.js.\n\n==================================================\nREQUIRED REPRODUCTION BEFORE EDITING\n==================================================\n\nFor every failed Luce test:\n\n1. reproduce the failure;\n2. identify exact event sequence;\n3. identify exact code path;\n4. identify whether failure is:\n   - xterm focus loss\n   - hidden textarea focus loss\n   - browser clipboard permission/focus condition\n   - stale renderer.js in live tab\n   - term.focus() restoration defect\n   - contextmenu handler defect\n   - keydown handler defect\n   - something else directly evidenced\n\nDo NOT patch based on theory alone.\n\n==================================================\nBOUNDARIES\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT:\n- rewrite server.js input handling\n- alter node-pty\n- alter OpenCode\n- add SendKeys\n- add PowerShell key injection\n- add Windows message injection\n- add OS-level clipboard automation\n- change seat registry\n- modify inbox/myDon work\n- renumber tiles\n- alter Seat 1 model\n- alter unrelated panes\n- intercept Ctrl+C\n- transform pasted text server-side\n- redesign terminal architecture\n\nPreserve:\n\nxterm\n→ WebSocket\n→ t.write()\n→ node-pty\n\n==================================================\nLIKELY REPAIR AREA\n==================