mains responsive\n\n==================================================\nSTATIC VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nRun:\n\nnode --check public\\renderer.js\n\nIf any other file is touched:\nrun node --check on that file too.\n\nDo not restart the whole DevPad unless required.\n\nIf only renderer.js changed:\nbrowser refresh should be sufficient unless direct evidence says otherwise.\n\n==================================================\nREQUIRED RETURN\n==================================================\n\nReturn exactly:\n\n1. STATUS:\n   PASS / PARTIAL / FAIL\n\n2. LUCE FAILURE REPRODUCED:\n   exact failed test(s)\n\n3. ROOT CAUSE:\n   exact client-side failure point\n\n4. FILES CHANGED:\n   exact paths\n\n5. CODE CHANGE:\n   concise before → after description\n\n6. WHY THIS IS MINIMUM:\n   explain why no broader change was required\n\n7. BEHAVIORAL MATRIX:\n   Ctrl+Shift+C\n   Ctrl+Shift+V\n   Shift+Insert\n   Right-click copy\n   Right-click paste\n   Ctrl+C interrupt\n   header/chrome focus recovery\n   Seat 1 multiline paste\n   cross-seat sanity\n   no regression\n\n8. STATIC VALIDATION:\n   node --check results\n\n9. CONFIRMATION:\n   Seat 1 still:\n   Coda\n   OpenCode\n   Big Pickle\n   tileId 1\n\n10. UNRELATED STATE:\n    confirm tiles 2–9 unchanged unless explicitly required\n\n11. REMAINING UNKNOWN / BLOCKER\n\n12. NEXT ROUTE:\n    Luce for independent verification\n    Don only after Luce passes\n\n==================================================\nHARD STOP\n==================================================\n\nIf current behavior already passes:\nDO NOT TOUCH CODE.\n\nIf failure cannot be reproduced:\nSTOP and return:\nNOT REPRODUCED — NO CHANGE MADE\n\nIf fix would require server.js / node-pty / OS input automation:\nSTOP and escalate to Don before broadening scope.\n\nSUCCESS CONDITION:\n\nDon can reliably copy and paste multiline prompts across DevPad terminal panes,\nincluding Seat 1 / Coda Big Pickle,\nwhile Ctrl+C still behaves as terminal interrupt\nand no unrelated DevPad architecture changes are introduced.\n```", "text_chars": 7318, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["C:\\Users\\Dekan", "public\\renderer.js", "renderer.js", "server.js"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6076bf05-dbdc-4bc0-b0cf-d1e20ac67311", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790291295.834, "updated_at": 1790291310.400555, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "so reemind me why we are doing all this ", "text_chars": 40, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "19dba216-950d-4082-9b29-c51cbec8b74a", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790291297.927155, "updated_at": 1790291308.785014, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Because we’re trying to **stop Don from being the operating system** for the whole GCE stack.\n\nRight now, too much of your workflow depends on you manually doing the glue work:\n\n- opening and arranging terminals\n- remembering which model is in which seat\n- copying prompts from me into terminals\n- moving results back\n- reopening sessions when a provider dies or credits run out\n- figuring out which seat should take the next step\n- managing ad hoc experiments separately from real project work\n- fighting focus, paste, browser, and window issues\n\nThe DevPad work is about turning that mess into a **stable operating environment**.\n\n### The big picture\n\n**Main DevPad**  \nYour serious project cockpit. Stable seats, stable identities, persistent work.\n\n**Rookie DevPad**  \nYour ad hoc / experimental cockpit. Cheap/free models, quick test