sion = PASS\n- ONLY remaining failure = Test 4, right-click copy with selection\n\n==================================================\nVERIFIED D-2 ROOT CAUSE\n==================================================\n\nNico's current fix snapshots selection at right-button mousedown.\n\nLuce proved this is too late.\n\nObserved sequence:\n\nshift+drag creates terminal selection\n→ mousemove occurs\n→ xterm destroys selection\n→ right-button mousedown occurs\n→ snapshot sees empty selection\n→ contextmenu falls into paste branch\n\nLuce variants:\n\nA.\nshift+drag\n→ right-click at drag endpoint with NO intervening mousemove\n→ selection alive\n→ COPY PASS\n\nB.\nshift+drag\n→ move pointer inside selection\n→ right-click\n→ selection already gone\n→ FAIL / paste branch\n\nC.\nshift+drag\n→ even same-coordinate/no-op mousemove\n→ right-click\n→ selection gone\n→ FAIL / paste branch\n\nTherefore:\n\nRIGHT-BUTTON MOUSEDOWN IS NOT EARLY ENOUGH.\n\n==================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nFix ONLY D-2.\n\nPreserve every currently passing behavior.\n\nExpected solution shape:\n\nCACHE THE LAST VALID NON-EMPTY TERMINAL SELECTION\nBEFORE THE DESTRUCTIVE MOUSEMOVE OCCURS.\n\nPreferred mechanism:\n\nterm.onSelectionChange(...)\n\nor another equally early xterm-native selection-change signal if direct code evidence shows it is safer.\n\nDo not build a broad mouse interception system unless required.\n\n==================================================\nRECOMMENDED DESIGN\n==================================================\n\nInside wireTermClipboard(term, el), maintain per-terminal selection cache.\n\nConceptual state:\n\nlastSelection = {\n  text,\n  at\n}\n\nWhen term selection changes:\n\n- if term.hasSelection()\n- read term.getSelection()\n- if non-empty\n- update lastSelection.text\n- update lastSelection.at\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT immediately erase the cache merely because xterm later reports empty selection as part of the destructive mousemove behavior we are specifically working around.\n\nAt contextmenu:\n\n1. ev.preventDefault()\n\n2. Determine whether a recently cached non-empty selection should be treated as the intended right-click-copy target.\n\n3. If valid/fresh:\n   - copy cached text verbatim\n   - consume cache one-shot\n   - do NOT invoke pasteClipboard()\n\n4. Otherwise:\n   - preserve existing right-click-with-no-selection behavior\n   - paste once\n   - refocus terminal\n\n==================================================\nSTALE-SELECTION SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nThis is critical.\n\nThe fix must NOT turn an ancient selection into a future accidental copy.\n\nPreserve or improve existing safety controls.\n\nUse bounded invalidation semantics such as:\n\n- freshness timeout\n- explicit left-click / non-right interaction invalidation\n- successful copy consumes cache\n- terminal-specific closure/state\n- new live selection replaces old cached selection\n\nDo NOT clear the cache merely because the destructive pre-contextmenu mousemove zeroes xterm selection.\n\nBut DO invalidate it when user intent clearly moves away from that selection.\n\nNico must reason carefully about event order.\n\n==================================================\nCROSS-TILE SAFETY\n==================================================\n\nSelection cache MUST remain per-terminal.\n\nNo global selection cache.\n\nA selection from Talon/Falcon/etc. must never be consumed by another tile's contextmenu handler.\n\nCurrent per-wireTermClipboard closure is preferred.\n\n==================================================\nPRESERVE D-1\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT regress the now-green paste fix.\n\nKeep:\n\nCtrl+Shift+V:\nev.preventDefault()\n→ navigator.clipboard.readText()\n→ term.paste()\n\nShift+Insert:\nev.preventDefault()\n→ navigator.clipboard.readText()\n→ term.paste()\n\nExpected behavioral target remains