eave debug noise in final code.\n\n==================================================\nDECISION BRANCH\n==================================================\n\nIF onSelectionChange proves reliable and early enough:\n- fix the specific implementation defect that prevented cache population.\n- preserve the existing architecture.\n\nIF onSelectionChange proves absent, late, or unusable:\n- stop relying on it for D-2.\n- implement capture-phase mousemove caching.\n\n==================================================\nPREFERRED FALLBACK — CAPTURE-PHASE MOUSEMOVE CACHE\n==================================================\n\nGoal:\ncapture the current non-empty selection BEFORE xterm's own mousemove handling destroys it.\n\nInside wireTermClipboard(term, el):\n\nAdd a CAPTURE-PHASE mousemove listener:\n\nel.addEventListener('mousemove', handler, true)\n\nImportant:\ncapture === true\n\nThe handler runs before descendant/xterm mousemove handlers.\n\nAt capture time:\n\n- if term.hasSelection()\n- get term.getSelection()\n- if non-empty\n- store it in per-terminal cache:\n  { text, at }\n\nThen allow event propagation normally.\n\nDO NOT:\n- preventDefault()\n- stopPropagation()\n- interfere with mouse movement\n- interfere with xterm selection behavior\n\nWe only observe/capture state early.\n\n==================================================\nCACHE RULES\n==================================================\n\nPer-terminal closure only.\n\nSET / REFRESH:\ncapture-phase mousemove sees non-empty selection\n→ cache exact text + timestamp\n\nALSO KEEP:\nright-mousedown snapshot if selection is still live\n→ Variant A remains supported\n\nCONTEXTMENU PRIORITY:\n\n1. fresh right-mousedown snapshot\n2. fresh pre-mousemove cache\n3. live selection fallback\n4. otherwise paste\n\nCONSUME:\nsuccessful right-click copy\n→ clear cache\n\nCtrl+Shift+C copy\n→ clear cache\n\nINVALIDATE:\nclear cache on a clearly new non-right click / user intent transition.\n\nEXPIRY:\nkeep bounded TTL.\n\