lenge\nSURFACE: OpenCode\nOCCUPANT MODEL: Space Bunny\nTILE ID: 3\n\nTILE 6\nSEAT: Nico\nIDENTITY: Nico\nROLE: Implementation / Builder\nSURFACE: OpenCode\nOCCUPANT MODEL: Space Bunny\nTILE ID: 6\n\nKimi subscription/runtime dependency for these two seats is RETIRED.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\nPROVIDER != SEAT.\nRUNTIME != SEAT.\n\nVittorio remains Vittorio.\nNico remains Nico.\nSpace Bunny is the occupant model.\n\nIDENTITY HOMES MUST BE PRESERVED.\n\n==================================================\nKNOWN CONFLICT\n==================================================\n\nA concurrent session was rewriting the same launch-chain files:\n\n- config.json\n- seats.js\n- adapter.js\n- adapters/opencode.js\n- server.js\n\nThat refactor introduced a buildLaunch(ctx) / runtime-root problem and temporarily broke seat launch.\n\nPrevious Nico correctly STOPPED rather than silently overwriting another session's work.\n\nDon's ruling:\n\n1. PRESERVE identity homes.\n2. DO NOT reinterpret or replace identity_home semantics.\n3. DO NOT reintroduce Kimi runtime dependencies.\n4. RESOLVE the active launch-chain refactor coherently.\n5. NO concurrent-write guessing.\n6. NO new architecture.\n7. NO new slice.\n8. ONE integrated recovery pass.\n\n==================================================\nFIRST ACTION — ESTABLISH CURRENT OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nBefore editing:\n\nInspect current mtimes/content/hashes of:\n\n- config.json\n- seats.js\n- adapter.js\n- adapters/opencode.js\n- server.js\n\nDetermine whether the concurrent refactor is still actively changing files.\n\nIF files are still being modified by another active process/session:\nSTOP.\n\nReturn:\nBLOCKED — ACTIVE CONCURRENT WRITER\n\nDo NOT race another writer.\n\nIF the refactor is no longer actively writing:\nYOU NOW OWN THE RECOVERY PASS.\n\nProceed.\n\n==================================================\nOBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nRestore one coherent DevPad launch chain so the ACTUAL board loads and seats launch correctly.\n\nRequired final operating state:\n\n1. Main DevPad loads.\n2. Board structure is coherent.\n3. Seat identities remain correct.\n4. Tile 3 launches:\n   Vittorio → OpenCode → Space Bunny\n5. Tile 6 launches:\n   Nico → OpenCode → Space Bunny\n6. No Kimi subscription/runtime dependency remains for tiles 3 or 6.\n7. Identity homes remain unchanged.\n8. Other seats continue using their configured identities/runtimes.\n9. Server is restarted onto the FINAL code, not stale modules.\n10. Don gets one runnable DevPad.\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT — 9 TILE VS 10 TILE DISCREPANCY\n==================================================\n\nOur authoritative Main DevPad frame is:\n\n1 Coda\n2 Chiave\n3 Vittorio\n4 Luce\n5 Don / VoiceBridge\n6 Nico\n7 Talon\n8 Keel\n9 Falcon\n\nNINE tiles.\n\nThe prior return mentioned \"all 10 tiles.\"\n\nDO NOT normalize this.\n\nInvestigate the current config/schema and determine:\n\n- Is there actually a 10th tile in the same Main DevPad?\n- Is the refactor operating on another DevPad/code path?\n- Is \"10 tiles\" merely an incorrect count?\n- Is there a hidden/service/non-board entry being counted?\n\nDo not redesign anything.\n\nJust establish the truth and preserve the authoritative Main DevPad unless Don has explicitly changed it elsewhere.\n\n==================================================\nLAUNCH-CHAIN RECOVERY\n==================================================\n\nFocus on the existing chain only:\n\nconfig\n→ seat definition\n→ surface/host/provider/model\n→ adapter/buildLaunch\n→ runtime root\n→ identity home\n→ OpenCode invocation\n→ PTY\n\nResolve the current ctx/runtime-root failure using the existing intended refactor.\n\nDo NOT:\n- invent a second launch system\n- add compatibility layers unless required\n- create new registry concepts\n- move identity directories\n- add provider inference\n- infer identity from model